MASTER PROJECT PROMPT: PIXELCRAFT UI
A Modern HTML & CSS Component Library — 15-Page Website Assignment
1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior UI/UX designer, frontend developer, design systems architect, technical SEO specialist, accessibility consultant, and web content strategist.

Design and build a complete, original, modern, responsive website called PixelCraft UI.

PixelCraft UI is a free HTML and CSS component library for students, beginner developers, freelance web designers, and frontend developers.

The website must be created specifically for an academic website design assignment. It must contain 15 distinct, properly connected HTML pages and use only HTML5 and CSS3 for its frontend implementation.

Do not create a generic template website. Build a cohesive, polished, premium-quality educational resource with a distinctive visual identity, realistic content, reusable components, and carefully designed layouts.

2. ASSIGNMENT REQUIREMENTS

The project must satisfy the following requirements:

Create 15 distinct HTML pages.
Use HTML5 and CSS3 only.
Use semantic HTML and clean, readable code.
Make every page responsive on desktop, tablet, and mobile.
Connect all relevant pages through working internal links.
Use a consistent design system throughout the website.
Include modern UI/UX patterns and accessible interactions.
Implement technical SEO and on-page SEO.
Structure content for answer engine optimization (AEO).
Follow generative engine optimization (GEO) best practices.
Include original, useful written content on every page.
Include a working CSS-only navigation experience.
Include print-friendly and code-example sections where appropriate.
Make the project easy to run locally by opening index.html.
